Some tips on sacrificing:

1)  Gods don't like old corpses.  This includes zombies, even if
freshly destroyed, and all other creatures (except, I think,
lizards--real lizards, not arbitrary :s) that have been dead for more
than a few rounds.  If your dog won't eat it, chances are your god
won't be charmed either (this is not quite true.  Your dog won't eat
poisonous corpses, like k's, which your god won't mind).

2)  The more impressive the kill, the more likely your god is to be
impressed.  Don't expect to get artifacts from sacrificing newts (you
can, in theory, but your chances are low).

3)  Unicorns of other alignments are especially appreciated.  This is
a great way to convert an alter, too.

4)  Sacrificing humans is not reccomended for non-chaotics.  It can be
risky business for chaotics, too, although it is a surefire way for
them to convert an altar.

5)  You won't get anything nifty from an alter unless your prayer
timeout has ended.  "You have a hopeful feeling"=Your timeout has
decreased.  "You have a feeling of reconcilliation"=Your timeout has
expired.
